%p
  Just a small and boring routine update to the website, this time around. We have moved from our previous hosting situation at heroku, to a new one, that I hope will serve the needs of this website while being easier on the wallet.
  
- unless intro
  %p
    I also took this opportunity as a good time to update a bunch of things on the backend. Many of the packages used in creating this version of the website hadn't been updated since it was first created
    = link_to("way back in 2019", "/posts/2019-10-21-new-website") + "."
    It's hard to believe it's been 7 years since then. The site has always had some tweaks to make interacting with it easier on mobile, but I was never super satisfied with how that looked and have taken the time to update that while I was at it as well.
  %p
    In all likelihood nobody else will notice much of a difference, especially in the desktop version, but that's to be expected from back-end changes like this. In any case, if you've never pulled up the site on a mobile device before, now is a great time to give it a try! And feel free to check out the major announcements from the last few posts there, while you are at it. See you next time!